{{!-- The season the steading is IN, as its own Seasons Change move performs it.

      This replaced two things: a "Turn to <next>" disclosure holding the INCOMING season's steps, and
      a "During <current>" section holding everything the current season owed. They were separate
      because turning happens once and the rest is used all season — but splitting them meant the
      numbered steps described a season the steading was not in, while every piece of state on the tab
      (the gain in force, the turnover checklist, the adjustments) belonged to the one it was. The box
      could be headed "Winter" with the line under it reading "Autumn, year 3".

      One box, and it is the current season's, so a step and the state that step produces are finally
      the same season's. Turning the wheel is the small control below it — the once-a-season act stays
      small, and the all-season surface is the large one.

      Params: seasons (SeasonsSnapshot). --}}
<section class="steading-season-box steading-block" data-season="{{seasons.turnover.season.key}}">

	<h3 class="steading-season-box-heading">
		{{!-- The season's glyph, tinted to the season it belongs to. Both the image and the tint come
		      from the `data-season` on this section — the stylesheet owns the four paths, because a
		      url() written here would be a document path resolved against the stylesheet, and an
		      install served under a route prefix would 404 on it. --}}
		<span class="steading-turn-glyph" aria-hidden="true"></span>
		<span class="steading-season-box-title">
			{{#if seasons.currentMove}}{{seasons.currentMove.name}}
			{{else}}{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.during"
			        season=(localize seasons.turnover.season.labelKey)}}{{/if}}
		</span>
	</h3>

	{{!-- The steps the move carries, in the order it gives them, each in the move's own words. The
	      tab used to draw Spring's — roll it, pick 1 gain, reset — for all four seasons, so winter's
	      opening 1d4+Population roll had no control and its +Fortunes roll, which is the FOURTH thing
	      winter does, was the one button at the top. --}}
	{{!-- The book's harvest plate rides BEHIND the steps, as a watermark in the bottom-right corner —
	      see `.steading-turn-steps::after`. The path arrives as a custom property because the
	      installer produces it at runtime; the stylesheet cannot write a url() it does not know.

	      Behind rather than beside: every arrangement that put the art IN the flow had to reconcile
	      its height against the steps' — a float cannot be bottom-aligned in CSS, so that took a
	      measured strut, a resize observer, and the result rows rebuilt out of grid so text could
	      wrap to the art's shape. As a background it participates in no layout at all.

	      Installer-provided and copyrighted, so absent in most worlds: with no property set, the
	      `var(--seasons-plate, none)` in the rule draws nothing. --}}
	{{#if seasons.steps.length}}
		<ol class="steading-turn-steps"
		    {{#if seasons.plate}}style="--seasons-plate: url('{{seasons.plate}}')"{{/if}}>
			{{#each seasons.steps}}
				{{> "stonetop.steading-turn-step"}}
			{{/each}}
		</ol>
	{{else}}
		<p class="stonetop-moves-empty">{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.movesEmpty"}}</p>
	{{/if}}

	{{!-- What the steading pays to keep what it has built. Outside the numbered steps because nothing
	      in Seasons Change says any of it — these are the steading's own bills, and reading them among
	      the move's own steps made them look like something the season did. --}}
	{{> "stonetop.steading-upkeep" statement=seasons.turnover.statement}}

	{{!-- What this steading's own buildings add to the season, under the steps that describe it.
	      Headed by the TRIGGER, in the book's own terms — "When winter comes" — so that no row under
	      it has to say when it fires.

	      Only where there is something left to say. Most of what a season brings is shown where it
	      happens now — in the step it bends, the result row it waits on, the step that generates it,
	      the bills above — and a heading over an empty list reads as a section that failed to load.
	      A season in which nothing fires at all still says so, which is not the same thing. --}}
	{{#if (or seasons.turnover.hasOwnClauses (not seasons.turnover.hasClauses))}}
	<div class="steading-during-owed">
		<h4 class="steading-during-label">
			{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.whenComes"
			           season=(localize seasons.turnover.season.labelKey)}}
		</h4>
		{{> "stonetop.steading-turnover" turnover=seasons.turnover}}
	</div>
	{{/if}}

	{{!-- The bends no step of this season claimed — the Golden Sapling's +1 on any generation, in a
	      season that generates nothing. Everything else hangs on the step it bends, up in the list. --}}
	{{> "stonetop.steading-adjustments" groups=seasons.adjustments.unclaimedGroups}}

	{{!-- The named points WITHIN the season that something built fires at — the harvest coming in, the
	      hunt being led. The sheet cannot know when those happen, so each is an offer the table takes
	      up rather than a schedule. Only moments something actually fires at appear.

	      And only the ones no step of the move numbers: autumn's fourth step IS the harvest, so what
	      fires at it is rolled and paid up there. What is left is the gathering at the inn, and a hunt
	      in a spring whose move does not name it. --}}
	{{#if seasons.unclaimedMoments.length}}
		{{> "stonetop.steading-moments" moments=seasons.unclaimedMoments}}
	{{/if}}

</section>

{{!-- Turning the wheel, and only that: it hands the steading the next season and posts nothing. The
      season's own Seasons Change is rolled from the box above, once the box is that season's — the
      card belongs after the steps it is step one of, not ahead of a season nobody has read yet. It
      asks before it fires, because the turn discards this season's checklist and gain. Outside the
      box because it is the one thing here that is not about the season the box is: it ends it. --}}
{{#if @root.editable}}
	<div class="steading-season-advance">
		<button type="button" class="steading-season-advance-button" data-action="turnSeason">
			<span>{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.seasonComes"
			      season=(localize seasons.turnover.next.labelKey)}}</span>
			<i class="fas fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		</button>
	</div>
{{/if}}
